  "name": "Chart grid layer",
  "description": "Grid lines as `chartGrid` layers. A grid layer draws in its chart's frame, not its own, so each resolves to the chart's frame; `draws` is true when its chart is in the shape and has readings. The first grid sits below a bar chart and stores nothing, so it resolves to 3 lines in white at 20 % (`#FFFFFF33`), 1 point thick. A line chart carries two more: 2 orange lines half a point thick, and one at the upper limits, 4 lines 4 points thick (clamping is pinned in each side's unit tests, since an out-of-range value cannot round-trip). The last grid links to a chart the document does not have, keeps its own frame and draws nothing.",
